She looked at me over her shoulder. The amber eyes. The copper hair. The sharp, striking face that was more beautiful to me now than any soft prettiness could ever be. She stood in the doorway of our room   the room we shared, the bed we shared, the life we shared without ever admitting that sharing it was a choice rather than a convenience.

<<dialog "Mira">>
Let's go kill some goblins.
<</dialog>>

I got dressed. Picked up the swords   mine and hers. Followed her downstairs and out the door into the rain and the dark and whatever came next.

We had a mine to clear.

---

[End of Day -2   Day -1 begins, The Greymire Mine. The goblins. The fall. The wound and Ysolde's vial, waiting in the dark like a seed waiting for soil.] */